customer: top_hat_man
problem: broken_hard_drive
daypart: midday
brief:
	A rich mogul (Cole Vanderbilt on his computer). He wants his hard drive replaced, won't say what's wrong with it, and insists that the old one is thrown away.

== drop-off
(neutral) Good day, dear sir. I come in a matter of great importance.
- Welcome to CompuFun!
- Tell me more and I'll see if I can help you.
(happy) I must say I really appreciate your store! So small and out of the way. Just perfect.
- Thanks, I guess...
- So, how can I help you?
(thinking) I really need to get my hard drive replaced.
- What's wrong with it?
	(angry) That's really none of your business! Prying like that will not get you far in life.
	- Oh, I'm sorry. I didn't mean to pry. Just trying to do my job.
	- Woha man, calm down.
	(neutral) Just change the hard drive. And don't forget to throw away the old one.
	- Don't worry we always throw away the parts we don't use.
